84,1086,1089,1092,1094,1097,1099],{"class":623,"line":1076},26,[621,1078,1079],{"class":787},"foreach",[621,1081,835],{"class":635},[621,1083,720],{"class":631},[621,1085,723],{"class":635},[621,1087,1088],{"class":631},"orders ",[621,1090,1091],{"class":635},"as",[621,1093,717],{"class":635},[621,1095,1096],{"class":631},"order",[621,1098,407],{"class":635},[621,1100,848],{"class":635},[621,1102,1104,1107,1109,1111,1113,1116],{"class":623,"line":1103},27,[621,1105,1106],{"class":726},"    echo",[621,1108,717],{"class":635},[621,1110,1096],{"class":631},[621,1112,723],{"class":635},[621,1114,1115],{"class":726},"invoiceUrl",[621,1117,777],{"class":635},[621,1119,1121],{"class":623,"line":1120},28,[621,1122,692],{"class":635},[189,1124,1125,1126,1128,1129,1131],{},"No VAT logic, no tax tables, no invoice templates, no client-side checkout widget to embed —\nthe checkout is a server-side redirect, like Stripe Checkout. See ",[227,1127,72],{"href":159},"\nand ",[227,1130,64],{"href":156}," for the full surface.",[258,1133],{},[261,1135,1137],{"id":1136},"feature-parity-and-whats-still-on-the-roadmap","Feature parity, and what's still on the roadmap",[189,1139,1140],{},"Vatly covers what a SaaS needs to start selling: subscriptions with trials, plan swaps,\ncancellation with grace and resume, one-off purchases, hosted checkout, refunds and chargebacks,\nand — because it's a Merchant of Record — VAT, invoicing and tax compliance handled for you. A\nfew capabilities you may use elsewhere aren't in the box yet. Here's the honest picture, and how\nto bridge it.",[266,1142,1143,1156],{},[269,1144,1145],{},[272,1146,1147,1150,1153],{},[275,1148,1149],{},"Capability",[275,1151,1152],{},"Vatly today",[275,1154,1155],{},"Notes",[292,1157,1158,1169,1181,1195,1204,1218,1234],{},[272,1159,1160,1163,1166],{},[297,1161,1162],{},"Subscriptions, trials, swap, grace, resume",[297,1164,1165],{},"✅",[297,1167,1168],{},"Full lifecycle, Cashier-shaped API",[272,1170,1171,1174,1176],{},[297,1172,1173],{},"One-off / multi-item checkout",[297,1175,1165],{},[297,1177,1178],{},[193,1179,1180],{},"checkout()->create(items: …)",[272,1182,1183,1186,1188],{},[297,1184,1185],{},"VAT, invoicing, tax remittance",[297,1187,1165],{},[297,1189,1190,1191,1194],{},"Handled — it's the point of a MoR. With Cashier (classic Stripe Billing) this is ",[206,1192,1193],{},"your"," job.",[272,1196,1197,1199,1201],{},[297,1198,540],{},[297,1200,1165],{},[297,1202,1203],{},"First-class models + events (more than most provide)",[272,1205,1206,1209,1211],{},[297,1207,1208],{},"Test / live segregation",[297,1210,1165],{},[297,1212,1213,1214,1217],{},"Every record carries ",[193,1215,1216],{},"testmode","; key prefix selects the mode",[272,1219,1220,1224,1227],{},[297,1221,1222],{},[211,1223,507],{},[297,1225,1226],{},"🔜 Roadmap",[297,1228,1229,1230,1233],{},"Until native codes land, model a promo as a dedicated ",[193,1231,1232],{},"subscription_plan_…"," at the discounted price and point that cohort at it. A couple of extra plans in the dashboard — not a blocker for launching offers.",[272,1235,1236,1240,1242],{},[297,1237,1238],{},[211,1239,524],{},[297,1241,1226],{},[297,1243,1244,1245,1247,1248,1251],{},"Vatly is built for SaaS, where entitlement follows subscription state — ",[193,1246,199],{}," ",[206,1249,1250],{},"is"," your license check. Per-seat keys for downloadable/offline software (Lemon Squeezy's signature feature) aren't here yet. If you ship license-activated desktop binaries, that's the one workflow to keep elsewhere for now.",[189,1253,1254],{},"The shape of the trade is deliberate: Vatly does the compliance-heavy core that's genuinely\nhard to build — being the seller of record, VAT across the EU, invoicing, disputes — and is\nfilling in the conveniences (coupons next) in the open. For a subscription SaaS selling into\nEurope and the world, there's enough here to launch today.",[258,1256],{},[261,1258,1260],{"id":1259},"why-teams-choose-vatly","Why teams choose Vatly",[189,1262,1263,1264,1267],{},"A Merchant of Record handles VAT, invoicing and tax remittance for you — and that part is now\ntable stakes. Paddle, Lemon Squeezy, Stripe Managed Payments and Vatly all do it; on Stripe it's\na flag on the request. So the real question isn't ",[206,1265,1266],{},"whether"," compliance is handled — it's whose\nentity you sell through:",[1269,1270,1271,1277,1283],"ul",{},[576,1272,1273,1276],{},[211,1274,1275],{},"Europe-first, by design."," EEA-based, EU jurisdiction, customer data kept in Europe. The other\nMoRs sit in the UK (Paddle) or the US (Lemon Squeezy, Stripe Managed Payments) — jurisdiction is\nthe one axis that genuinely separates them, and the reason Vatly exists.",[576,1278,1279,1282],{},[211,1280,1281],{},"No exposure to US policy."," Your seller-of-record relationship and your customers' data stay\nunder EU law — a clean answer when an enterprise buyer, or your own board, asks where they sit.",[576,1284,1285,1288],{},[211,1286,1287],{},"One familiar API."," The Cashier-shaped surface means there's little to learn and little to\nrewrite.",[246,1290,1291],{},[189,1292,1293],{},[211,1294,1295],{},"You Just Ship.",[258,1297],{},[261,1299,1301],{"id":1300},"next-steps","Next steps",[1269,1303,1304,1314,1322],{},[576,1305,1306,1309,1310,1313],{},[211,1307,1308],{},"Starting fresh"," → ",[227,1311,1312],{"href":150},"Getting started"," wires up the trait, config, migrations and\nwebhook in a few minutes.",[576,1315,1316,1309,1319,1321],{},[211,1317,1318],{},"Already running another provider",[227,1320,172],{"href":173},"\nshows how to add Vatly beside your current biller and migrate customers over gradually.",[576,1323,1324,1309,1327,1329,1330,1329,1332,1329,1334,1329,1336,1329,1338],{},[211,1325,1326],{},"Reference",[227,1328,176],{"href":177}," · ",[227,1331,56],{"href":153},[227,1333,64],{"href":156},[227,1335,72],{"href":159},[227,1337,80],{"href":162},[227,1339,38],{"href":165},[189,1341,1342,1343,1346,1347,1346,135